nd shown that coherent states are maximal for the particular environment model examined. To generalize these results, I consider entropy production within the Lindblad theory of open systems, treating environment effects perturbatively. I characterize the maximally predicitive states which emerge from several forms of effective dynamics, including decoherence from spatially correlated noise. Under a variety of conditions, coherent states emerge as the maximal states.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "arXiv"}}], "refereed": true, "primary_arxiv_category": ["quant-ph"], "external_system_identifiers": [{"schema": "ADS", "value": "1996PhRvA..53..655G"}, {"schema": "SPIRES", "value": "SPIRES-3167704"}, {"schema": "MSNET", "value": "1372496"}], "titles": [{"title": "The Emergence of classicality via decoherence described by Lindblad operators"}, {"source": "arXiv", "title": "The Emergence of Classicality via Decoherence Described by Lindblad Operators"}], "facet_author_name": ["2432745_Michael R. Gallis"], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:396421", "updated": "2026-02-06T09:33:12.959774"}, "curated": true, "journal_title_variants": ["Phys.Rev.A", "Phys. Rev. A"], "arxiv_eprints": [{"categories": ["quant-ph", "gr-qc", "hep-th"], "value": "quant-ph/9506019"}]}, "id": "396421", "updated": "2026-02-06T09:33:12.959774+00:00", "created": "1995-06-22T00:00:00+00:00", "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/396421?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/396421?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/396421?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/396421?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/396421?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/396421?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A396421"}}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net